toolkit-opbench
==============

This project's DESIGN is informed by NVIDIA/SOL-ExecBench
(https://github.com/NVIDIA/SOL-ExecBench, Apache-2.0).

What we borrowed (ideas and data format only, no source code copied):
  - the problem packaging layout: definition (symbolic axes + IO specs +
    reference + tolerance) separated from workloads (concrete shapes)
  - the concept of reward-hack detection as a first-class evaluator
    concern (monkey-patched timers, injected threads, lazy tensors,
    replaced eval functions)
  - timing discipline: per-iteration cache flush, fixed warmup and
    iteration counts, median-based reporting
  - keeping the "reference baseline" timing out of the default run path
    because it can dominate total evaluation time

What we did NOT take:
  - SOL-Score and its B200 roofline (SOLAR). Our denominators are
    measured on Hygon DCU (gfx938) and are kept in our own constants file.
  - their problem dataset, reference implementations, or descriptions.
    Those are copyrighted and also hardware-specific.

Our task taxonomy (including the L5 counterfactual tier and the
three-arm comparison), the scoring model, and all code in this repository
are original work.
